# Round 63: an accepted outward write lands in the NAME's observation
# regime, not the writer-function's. setv does not observe, so its
# emission ran with the per-function g_observed off and its outward store
# to demoted module v was a plain env store -- no observer-slot update.
# The value was right and the observer verdict wrong: VM `5 / moving`,
# AOT `5 / equilibrium`, both rc 0. Seven rounds had hardened ORDER on
# the outward arms; none asked which REGIME the accepted write lands in.
# g_outward_obs now carries the decl loop's verdict to the assign arms,
# which use aot_observe_num/_val for these names.
v is 0
define setv(k) as:
    v is k
    return k
setv of 5
print of v
print of (report of v)
v is "s"
